// ================================================================================================
//  ANIMATED CREATURES: every example enemy in the game, in one file.
//
//  Layout:   "collections": [ { "collection": <name>, "enemy": [ <enemy>, ... ] }, ... ]
//  A battle picks an enemy by collection + enemyID, e.g. in a battleset wave:
//      { "collection": "enemyCollection01", "enemyID": 4 }
//  so keep collection names as they are, and keep enemyIDs unique inside a collection.
//
//  Add an enemy:      copy one inside the right collection; give it a new enemyID (highest + 1).
//  Order inside a collection doesn't matter: enemies are grouped by family, found by enemyID.
//  Add a new area:    add another { "collection": ..., "enemy": [...] } block below.
//  Every field:       datafiles/README.md -> Enemies.
//  Comments:          // works on its own line or after a value (the game strips them).
//  Summary lines:     #id Name | HP | ATK | Lv  -  what it does each turn
// ================================================================================================
